@@ -10,3 +10,8 @@ Run its tests with `npm test`.
 Each added task has a stable string `id`, unique within its list. Renaming a task keeps its ID. Use
 `list.get(id)` to retrieve a task by ID; `find`, `complete`, `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and
 `remove` accept either an ID or the task's current title. IDs are assigned in add order within a list.
+
+Each task records `createdAt` and `updatedAt` as ISO-8601 date-time strings. A new task starts with
+matching timestamps. Completing, reopening, renaming, tagging or untagging a task updates `updatedAt`
+when the operation changes it. `createTodoList` accepts an optional timestamp function, which defaults
+to the current time, so callers can provide a deterministic clock when needed.
